{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: identical if/else branches in `matchedArtifactFile`**

Both branches of the inner conditional produce byte-identical results:

```javascript
if (left.slice(-1) === '/' && right.charAt(0) === '/') {
    file = left + '<KEY>' + right;
} else {
    file = left + '<KEY>' + right;   // same expression as the if-branch
}
```

Preserving this verbatim (with the documenting comment) was the right call under gh-1085's "no code path removed" rule — noted and appreciated. Since the two branches are literally the same expression, collapsing them to a single `file = left + '<KEY>' + right;` is provably behavior-identical; a good follow-up cleanup (the comment above it can then explain the quirk without the dead conditional).
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment1.md"}

{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: unchecked `ACTION_SKIP_LOGS` lookup can mask a future skip as a hard failure**

```javascript
ACTION_SKIP_LOGS[inputs.reason]();
```

If a new reason is ever added to `resolveActionInputs` without a matching `ACTION_SKIP_LOGS` entry, this throws a `TypeError`, and the outer `catch` in `action()` converts what should be a benign config-skip into `{ success: false, error }`.

Unreachable today (both maps are private to this file and sit ~140 lines apart), so informational only. A defensive lookup keeps the mapping total:

```javascript
var log = ACTION_SKIP_LOGS[inputs.reason];
if (log) log();
```
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment2.md"}

{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: "Pure precondition ladder" comment is inaccurate for `resolveActionInputs`**

The doc comment says:

```javascript
// Pure precondition ladder — every gate the action must pass before any
// upload happens, ...
```

…but the function also performs I/O-bound resolution: `releaseArtefacts.resolveArtefactRepository(customParams)` and `configLoader.loadProjectConfig(ctx.actualParams)` hit SCM/config discovery in production. The risk is a future maintainer hoisting this call out of the `try`/`catch`, caching it, or calling it speculatively under a "it's pure, no side effects" assumption.

Consider rewording, e.g. "Precondition ladder — every gate the action must pass before any upload happens (the artefact-repo and project-config resolution steps may perform I/O)."
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment3.md"}

